title: Denial Intelligence › Peer-to-peer › Brief buttons
route: /denials/D-3318/brief
intro: The buttons on the brief page: 'Copy brief' and 'Print' (off in the hosted preview), and the call-time button. Recording the outcome has its own diagram.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "The brief page is open"

click c1 "Click 'Copy brief'"
process p1 "The whole brief becomes plain text\nOpening, points, what they may say, the ask, dates, numbers, documents"
decision d1 "Does the browser allow copying?"
process p2 "Fallback: a hidden text box and the copy command, for pages opened as files"
decision d2 "Did the fallback work?"
toast t1 "'Brief copied'\n'Paste it into your notes before the call.'"
toast t2 "'Could not copy'\n'Select the text on the page and copy it instead.'"

click c2 "Click 'Print'"
decision d3 "Is this the hosted preview?"
toast t3 "'Print is off in this preview'\n'Open the single-file version of the demo to use it.'"
process p3 "The browser print dialog opens"
process p4 "Print layout hides the sidebar, top bar and buttons; only the brief is printed"
doc dc1 "Paper or PDF copy of the brief"

click c3 "Click 'Book the call' (or 'Change the call time' once booked)"
goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Peer-to-peer › Book the call"
click c4 "Click 'Record the call outcome'"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Peer-to-peer › Record the call outcome"
click c5 "Tick a box under 'Have these open'"
store st1 "Tick saved on the denial\nThe box stays ticked next time"
click c6 "Click the crumb 'Denial Intelligence'"
goto g3 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened"
end e1 "Notes are in the clipboard"
end e2 "Brief is on paper"
endx e3 "Nothing was copied"
endx e4 "Nothing was printed"

s1 --> c1 & c2 & c3 & c4 & c5 & c6
c1 --> p1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| t1 --> e1
d1 -->|No| p2 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| t1
d2 -->|No| t2 --> e3
c2 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| t3 --> e4
d3 -->|No| p3 --> p4 --> dc1 --> e2
c3 --> g1
c4 --> g2
c5 --> st1
c6 --> g3
